Inside a projected index
description: the index_editing state
- >
  The `[` and `]` are in the cell with the caret between them - the index digits (or the `?`
  position wildcard) type inside. This is cell_editing wearing brackets; the same filter and
  dropdown scheduling applies
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Event
      width: 2
    - 'Condition / note'
      width: 4
    - 'Next state'
      width: 2
  - ['`alphanumeric`', '', '`index_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`close_bracket`', '', '[cell_editing](*::server:query-editor:cell_editing)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'the pair is empty - it dismantles', '[cell_editing](*::server:query-editor:cell_editing)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'otherwise', '`index_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`colon`', '', '[cell_editing](*::server:query-editor:cell_editing)']
  - ['`escape`', '', '[idle_path](*::server:query-editor:idle_path)']
